Spec: VersionCmd

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Back the `agent version` sub-command: a clap leaf that prints the single workspace
    version constant and exits. Its only job is to keep the release version observable
    from the agent binary.

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap `Args` derive, empty field list; `Debug`. Consumed by
    ./main.sdd under the `Version` subcommand.
  @run — takes `&Parameters` by reference, ignores it entirely, prints
    `common::vynilpackage::VERSION` followed by a newline to stdout via `println!`,
    returns `()` with no failure path.

Accepts:
  `&Parameters` — structurally required for dispatch symmetry with the sibling
    sub-commands; value never read.

Returns:
  `()`. No @Result, no exit call, no error channel: the command always succeeds.

Must:
  Print exactly the @common::vynilpackage::VERSION string frozen in
    ../common/src/vynilpackage.sdd, nothing else, no prefix or suffix beyond the
    newline @println! appends.
  Take the value from the shared @common constant rather than a local `env!` crate
    version, so agent and every other binary report one identical version string.

Depends on:
  ../common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — the VERSION constant.
  ./main.sdd — the only caller, synchronous arm of the dispatch table.

Scenario: version prints the shared constant
  Given `VersionCmd` with any empty @Parameters
  When @run is invoked
  Then stdout holds the @common::vynilpackage::VERSION line and nothing else
  And the call returns without touching stdout/stderr configuration or the process exit code

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide later whether `version` should also print per-crate versions or a git
      commit; the sub-command flag surface is deliberately empty today.

Done when:
  The command keeps printing the shared VERSION constant byte-for-byte.
